1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,400
Allergic rhinitis — if your sneezing and runny nose just got worse this month, here's why.

2
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:12,160
Ragweed season is starting right now, and there's a good chance you've been treating it wrong.

3
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:16,160
Here's what's actually happening and what genuinely helps.

4
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:25,920
Ragweed pollen allergy affects more than 23 million people in the US, and nearly 50 million experience symptoms from it in late summer and fall.

5
00:00:26,240 --> 00:00:32,480
It's responsible for about half of all pollen-related allergic rhinitis cases in North America.

6
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:41,520
Ragweed season begins in early August, peaks in mid-September through October, and tapers off after the first frost.

7
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:46,880
One thing you've probably heard doesn't actually work: local honey.

8
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:52,800
The idea is that eating local honey builds tolerance to the pollen making you sneeze.

9
00:00:53,120 --> 00:01:01,680
But bees collect large, heavy flower pollen that barely becomes airborne, while ragweed pollen is small and wind-blown.

10
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,080
It's a completely different pollen.

11
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:10,480
A controlled study found daily local honey gave no real improvement over a placebo.

12
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:12,000
Here's the mechanism.

13
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:20,240
When ragweed pollen lands on your nasal lining, your immune system misreads it as a threat and releases histamine.

14
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:31,200
Histamine widens blood vessels and irritates nerve endings, which is why you get sneezing, a runny nose, congestion, and itchy eyes all at once.

15
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:33,680
Three things genuinely help.

16
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:42,000
Nasal saline irrigation, a HEPA air filter used the right way, and knowing when an antihistamine is worth it.

17
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:45,280
First, nasal saline irrigation.

18
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:57,760
Hypertonic saline rinses physically flush pollen out of your nasal passages, and studies show they lower nasal symptom scores and cut how much rescue antihistamine people need.

19
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:03,280
Second, a HEPA air filter, but keep your expectations realistic.

20
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:15,120
It reduces airborne particles by close to 70%, which helps your bedroom air overall, though some studies found it didn't fully eliminate sneezing and congestion on its own.

21
00:02:15,440 --> 00:02:19,520
Pair it with saline rinses rather than relying on it alone.

22
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:25,360
Third, an over-the-counter non-drowsy antihistamine works well for most people.

23
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:36,880
If symptoms last past a few weeks despite that, or you're missing sleep over it, see a doctor about a prescription nasal steroid spray instead of just pushing through it.

24
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:46,640
Nasal saline irrigation, a HEPA filter as backup, and the right antihistamine genuinely cut ragweed symptoms down.

25
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:58,480
If your symptoms drag on for over a month or start affecting your sleep and focus, don't just wait it out — see an allergist and get tested for what's actually triggering it.
